<title>USA: TABLE - Hollywood Theaters sells 144a notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Hollywood Theaters sells 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Hollywood Theaters Inc was priced in private placement market on Thursday, via lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co, according to a market soource.</p>
<p>BORROWER</p>
<p>AMT $110 MLN	 COUPON 10.625 PCT MATURITY 8/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B3    YIELD  10.625 PCT PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-MINUS   SPREAD +460 BPS   CALLABLE  NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTES: The notes have a three-year equity call for $33 million at 110.625. ((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
